-- Whose Clauses (ADR 0074): the chunks whose condition holds.

-- Lists of maps, by a key of `it`.
on sort orders, tickets
  put every item of orders whose the amount of it > 100 GBP into big
  put the first item of tickets whose the status of it is "open" into next
  put the last item of tickets whose it's status is "closed" into done
  put the third item of orders whose the amount of it > 10 GBP and it's paid into third
end sort

-- Text chunks give lists of texts, and every ordinal is a match position.
on scan report
  put every line of report whose the length of it > 80 into long
  put every word of line 2 of report whose it begins with "a" into aWords
  put every item of report delimited by ";" whose it is not empty into fields
  put the first item of report delimited by ";" whose it contains "x" into firstX
  put every character of report whose it is in "aeiou" into vowels
  put every code point of report whose it is not " " into points
end scan

-- A Whose Clause is a whole Expression, and its condition runs to the next
-- top-level comma, bracket or `into`.
on shapes xs, n
  put [every item of xs whose it > n, the last item of xs whose it < 0] into pair
  put the length of (every item of xs whose it > n) into count
  if (the first item of xs whose it > n) is empty then put 0 into count
  put every item of xs whose (every item of it whose it > 0) is not empty into nested
  return every item of (1..n) whose it mod 2 = 0
end shapes

-- `whose` is a Name elsewhere, and a chunk index named `whose` needs brackets.
on names whose
  put whose + 1 into every
  put item (whose) of [1, 2] into one
  put every into item
end names
